{
  "format": "newton-scene",
  "version": 2,
  "meta": {
    "name": "Driven harmonic oscillator",
    "source": "demo",
    "demoId": "driven-harmonic-oscillator",
    "description": "Horizontal spring–mass with a chirped drive F(t) = 2 sin(ω(t) t) along +x, where ω(t) = 2π(0.4 + 0.01t) rad/s. m = 1 kg, k = 40 N/m ⇒ f₀ = √(k/m)/(2π) ≈ 1.01 Hz. Light linear damping (frictionAir) so a steady amplitude develops. Equilibrium at x = 0 m. To plot a resonance curve: open Graph → Advanced — parameter sweep → Independent = f (drive), Dependent = Aₓ (steady), From ≈ 0.4 Hz, To ≈ 1.6 Hz, Runs ≈ 21."
  },
